Use the built-in overworld debug menu to jump straight to the lab.

1. Build/run a non-release ROM, then press R + Start while in the overworld. The debug menu is enabled by default outside release builds.
2. Select Flags & Vars… → Set Var XYZ… and set:
•  VAR_WESTLOCK_LIBRARY_STATE  ( 0x40F9 , decimal 16633) to 1.
3. Ensure the Pokédex has not already been received:
• Flags & Vars… → Set Flag XYZ…
• Select  FLAG_SYS_POKEDEX_GET  ( 0x0861 , decimal 2145).
• The menu shows whether it is  TRUE  or  FALSE ; press A only if it is  TRUE , to toggle it off.
4. Optionally set  FLAG_SYS_POKEMON_GET  ( 0x0860 , decimal 2144) and use Give X… to add a Pokémon, so the save resembles the real story state.
5. Select Utilities… → Warp to map warp…, then enter:
• Map group: 34
• Map: 2 ( MAP_LARCH_LAB_INSIDE )
• Warp: 0 or 1

Give X… → Pokémon…
Select a species, choose its level, then confirm to add it to the party.

Also set the system flag so the party menu behaves normally:

Flags & Vars… → Set Flag XYZ… →  FLAG_SYS_POKEMON_GET 
That is flag  0x0860  (decimal 2144). Toggle it to  TRUE .

For your Larch scene test, use Give X… → Pokémon… to add any Pokémon, set:

•  VAR_WESTLOCK_LIBRARY_STATE  ( 0x40F9  / decimal 16633) →  1 
•  FLAG_SYS_POKEMON_GET  →  TRUE 
•  FLAG_SYS_POKEDEX_GET  →  FALSE 
